/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 33 632 [
[(In Pd, most objects carry out their functions when they get)]
[(messages in their leftmost inlets, and their other inlets are)]
[(for storing values that can modify the next action. Here, the)]
[([+] object does its thing only when the left-hand input changes.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 39 415 [
[(In Pd you must sometimes think about what order an object is going)]
[(to get its messages in. If an outlet is connected to more than one)]
[(inlet it's undefined which inlet will get the cookie first. I've)]
[(rigged this example so that the left-hand side box gets its inputs)]
[(in the good, right-to-left order, so that the hot inlet gets hit)]
[(when all the data are good. The "bad adder" happens to receive its)]
[(inputs in the wrong order and is perpetually doing its addition)]
[(before all the data are in. There's a [trigger] object that exists)]
[(solely to allow you to control message order explicitly:)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 46 104 [
[(A [trigger] takes any number of "bang" and "float" arguments)]
[(\050among others\051. The object and arguments can be abbreviated with)]
[(the first letter. It sequences messages in right-to-left order.)]
[(Hook it to two inputs without crossing the wires and you get the)]
[(expected result. Cross the wires and you get a memory effect.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 237 549 [
[(Here's the downside:)]
[(drag this -->)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
